# Gentian OS installer configuration. Non-secret; credentials never go here.
#
#   cp install.env.template install.env    # edit, then ./install.sh
#
# This file says how to RUN the install. What the cluster IS lives on the
# Cluster claim in gentian-deployments, which the install writes, commits and
# pushes as its step 0 when it is absent -- every setting asked, with its
# default. Credentials are prompted for and stored in OpenBao. See
# docs/install-reference.md §4.

# ── Set these ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Directory name under clusters/ in gentian-deployments, and half the Cluster
# claim's name. Set it before the first run; step 0 pushes the tree it names.
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_CLUSTER_ID=default-cluster
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_STAGE=dev

GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_REPO=https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-deployments
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_BRANCH=main

# The gentian-os ref every in-cluster Application tracks. A release tag pins the
# cluster; a branch follows it. docs/deployment.md §4.
GENTIAN_OS_BRANCH=develop

# ── Defaults — change for a fork or a mirror ─────────────────────────────────

GENTIAN_OS_REPO=https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-os

# The user interface: where it comes from, and the ref the cluster follows.
GENTIAN_UI_BRANCH=develop
GENTIAN_UI_REPO=https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-ui

# How each repository authenticates: none | basic | bearer. The platform's own
# are public; set one to basic or bearer only for a mirror that asks for a
# login. Deployments defaults to basic because a private
# repository cannot describe its own access; set none for a public one.
GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_AUTH=basic
GENTIAN_UI_AUTH=none
GENTIAN_OS_AUTH=none
GENTIAN_OS_IMAGE_REPOSITORY=ghcr.io/gentian-org/gentian-os

# 0 when cert-manager, CloudNativePG and Reloader are managed elsewhere.
INSTALL_CLUSTER_INFRA=1

# 1 in CI: take the default for every prompt instead of asking.
GENTIAN_NONINTERACTIVE=0

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GENTIAN_DEPLOYMENTS_PATH=${HOME}/.gentian/gentian-deployments
# Local checkout of the deployments repository.

# KERNEL_DOMAIN=platform.example.com
# Only for a non-interactive first run. The Cluster claim owns the domain, and
# step 0 asks for it; a value here after that overrides the claim.

# CLUSTER_ADMIN_RECOVERY_EMAIL=you@example.org
# Where the platform admin's activation link (and later a password
# reset) is mailed. The account has no password until its holder sets one
# through that single-use link. Unset, the handover asks; left empty there,
# the link is shown in the terminal once instead. Kept here, not in git: a
# person's address in a repository outlives the account.

# TENANCY_MODE=multi
# Only for a non-interactive first run; step 0 asks otherwise, and the Cluster
# claim owns it afterwards (spec.tenancyMode). multi, the default: the platform
# tenant plus any number of user tenants, each at desktop.<tenant>.<kernel-
# domain>, created after the install by the platform admin. single: the
# platform tenant plus exactly one user tenant, named user, on the cluster's
# own addresses (desktop.<kernel-domain>); the install creates it after the
# handover. Either way the platform admin signs in at platform.<kernel-domain>.
# docs/install-reference.md §4.

# SECRET_MODE=derived
# Only for a non-interactive first run; step 0 asks otherwise, and the Cluster
# claim owns it afterwards (spec.secretMode). derived, the default: every
# credential the platform generates is computed from the master password and
# the salt, so a rebuild from the recovery kit arrives at the same values.
# random: each is drawn once and kept only in OpenBao (an app's own secrets
# and two kernel values stay derived). Nothing backs OpenBao up: if its
# storage is lost on a running cluster, random credentials cannot be made
# again, so such a cluster has to snapshot OpenBao itself. Choose the mode
# before the first install: changing it later leaves every existing
# credential as it is. docs/design/security.md §6.

# OPENBAO_CLI_VERSION=v2.5.0
# Which `bao` to fetch when none is on PATH. Unset takes the versions.yaml pin.

# GENTIAN_OS_IMAGE_TAG=develop-1a2b3c4
# Leave unset: the installer then runs the image CI built from the commit this
# checkout is on (<branch>-<short-sha>; a release tag gives its version). A
# value set here is used as it stands and takes precedence over image.tag in
# the cluster's values file, so a line left from an earlier install keeps the
# cluster on that older build. docs/install-reference.md §4, "Image tags".

# PORTAL_IMAGE_TAG=develop
# The branch whose charts are installed for the platform's own apps: the
# desktop, the administration console, the sign-in page and the App Store app.
# Match the branch gentian-ui published from.

# INFRA_CHART_REPO=oci://registry.example.com/charts
# Mirror for the infrastructure charts, instead of their upstream repositories.

# INFRA_CHART_PRIVATE=false
# true when that mirror needs the infra-chart-registry credential.

# CROSSPLANE_ACTIVATE_ALL=true
# Install every resource type of every Crossplane provider (several hundred
# CRDs), as installs did before. Unset, only the types the platform uses exist
# (crossplane/providers/activation.yaml). Set it, and run the installer again,
# if a fresh install waits on a resource type that list lacks; it cannot be
# taken back on that cluster (docs/install-reference.md, "Provider resource
# types").

# KERNEL_NETWORK_POLICIES=true
# The kernel namespaces refuse a connection their NetworkPolicies do not list.
# Off unless true. Turn it on after a successful install, with
# ./install.sh --only A-01,B-01, and off again the same way if a component
# then times out reaching another (docs/install-reference.md, "When something
# is wrong").

# GENTIAN_NO_LICENCE_REPORT=1
# Turn the licence report off (the same as --no-licence-report). By default the
# cluster tells the report address once a day what it runs: its tenants, how
# many accounts each has, and the apps installed through the App Store. No
# personal data. Off, nothing is sent and the App Store is not offered.

# GENTIAN_LICENCE_REPORT_URL=https://reports.example.org/licence-reports
# Send the licence report somewhere other than the default address.

# GENTIAN_GPG_HOME=${HOME}/.gentian/gnupg
# Where the two deployment signing keys live. Never your own keyring.

# GENTIAN_KIT_INCLUDE_BREAK_GLASS=1
# 0 keeps the break-glass signing key out of the recovery kit. Then only this
# host can write to the deployments repository when the director cannot.

# GENTIAN_KIT_RECIPIENT=age1...
# An age public key to encrypt the recovery kit to, for an unattended install
# where nobody can type a passphrase.

# GENTIAN_NO_CREDENTIAL_CACHE=1
# Keep typed credentials in the process only; retype them on a resumed run.
